GothiviaPage: {
	DisplayName: Gothivia Iyx, 3-Shot Wonder
	WhereToFind: The familial bond is a strong one, isn't it?
	Lore: Gothivia grew up under the mother of blood, sanguimi, and although when she was born she had no power, she was always a very great strategist as well as being one of the nicest people to ever come across. As she grew up with her sister Verlia and her adopted sister Irradia, she befriended animals and took charge of the Ghetsis before punkertown was made on top of it. She was able to feel animals in a way which led her to grow a sense of naturality to the environment around her. She started to grow a tree in her childhood which held great importance to her throughout her life that was supposed to feed the life around, the tree would be deemed the “Tree of life.” It was made off the edge of her town, Ghetsis. During her youth, Zui would travel frequently to check up on the village as it was one of her first expeditions to an area of teaching magic, everyone loved her, but Zui took special interest in Gothivia. She had no powers at the time, and despite that cared down to the core about everything around her, no need for rule, and dreamed big with no magic, reminding Zui of herself. Zui dedicated her time to training Gothivia to learn growth magic, but she had almost no affinity to actually learning it, but instead her body really only allowed her to use radiance. It was almost like a curse, and as she learned she realized she was only to grow into the thing that would tear her dreams apart. Gothivia had an affinity for radiance magic, or fire magic to say, the most out of anyone ever, almost aside from Zui. Gothivia after learning magic would eventually cast herself out, she didn’t want to burn the things she very much loved, she resigned control over the Ghetsis, especially since there was a sort of industrialization coming across to her village, she couldn’t bear it any longer and she asked Zui to help her release her magic. It was too strong for her, she would burn everything she touched, scorched to a crisp. Gothivia, while being a late teen, had left her town and her family to keep them all safe until she could rid or control her powers. Going with Zui to the Cinderspark, or what she called, the dragon’s lair. As she was down there, she felt a bit more akin to being at home, being in an environment that could handle the heat and she was able to train her power to learn to control it. Warming and befriending many fiery animals as well as dragons, Gothivia found a dragon that was particularly fond of sparring her. It was a strange dragon with such tiny wings it almost looked like a snake, she named this Rek. Zui and Gothivia were able to get along very well and became great friends together as they trained for many many years, Zui would go back and forth to the surface and come to tell uplifting stories to Gothivia without shedding the details of the war happening above ground. Gothivia would eventually return to the surface after learning how to finally control her power. When she returned, nothing was the same. Her sister had disappeared, her town flooded with junk and ruined as Irradia had taken control of the new place named Punkertown, and her tree. It had grown so much it had become a staple of the world where people would visit. She was happy, furious and sad all at the same time, and eventually broke down. She wanted to look for her sister but had no clue where to go, what to do. She had felt hopeless as she would sit underneath the tree wondering what to do. People would come and spectate as there was a flame-like serpent dragon, being Rek, who would follow her everywhere. Some people would even try to claim her as a God, as they passed or even challenged her, as she had looked so different from what she had been as a kid. She randomly disappeared into the night and came back with wings, and a dragon who protected her. As people challenged her, Rek would usually step in to blast people away but if they had ever had the chance to fight Gothivia while she was sad, she would usually let anger out upon them, killing many. She had no intention of doing this but not being in the right headspace did this to her. She had become so powerful, that those who challenged her were given 2 warning shots and a killing blow. One day Irradia caught wind of her sister acting tenacious and took a visit, but Gothivia was disappointed in letting their home be turned into a junkyard or what they called “Vilepipes,” now. Gothivia just wanted things to go back to the way they were but Irradia couldn’t tear down what she and her cousin had built. Neither was happy with the results of their labor and they agreed to make up, but still sulk a bit to this day about their lost sister, trying to figure out what happened to her.
}

